# Build-context exclusions for deploy/docker/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit looks for "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore" before falling back to
# "<context>/.dockerignore". That matters here: the build context is the
# workspace PARENT directory (~/projs/go/church), which is not a git repo, so
# a .dockerignore placed there could not be version-controlled or reviewed.
# Keeping it beside the Dockerfile puts it inside the church repo instead.
#
# Requires DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 (or docker buildx) — the classic builder ignores
# this file. deploy.sh enforces that.
#
# Without these rules the context is ~2.9 GB and, worse, carries each site's
# live credentials into the build cache.

# --- Never, under any circumstances -------------------------------------
# Live site config: Stripe keys, SMTP passwords, object-store credentials.
# These reach the pod through the <site>-config Secret, never through a layer.
**/cfg/options.yml
**/cfg/random_seeds.txt
**/token.txt

# --- Bulk: not build inputs ---------------------------------------------
church_mobile/          # Flutter app, ~2.6 GB — unrelated to the server image
*.zip                   # archived legacy projects (~53 MB)
**/node_modules/        # SCSS/Stylus toolchain; dist/ is built before packaging
**/sermons/             # cema/sermons is ~92 MB of media; served from IDrive e2
**/dump.rdb             # leftover from the retired Redis session store
**/.git/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store

# --- Build/run artifacts that must not leak into the image --------------
**/log/*
!**/log/.keep
# Locally-compiled site binaries: darwin/arm64 here, useless and confusing in
# a linux image, and they would defeat the layer cache on every rebuild.
ccswm/ccswm
cema/cema
# Admin-uploaded article images live on the data volume in k8s; a stale local
# copy baked into the image would be shadowed by the mount anyway.
**/dist/img/*
!**/dist/img/.keep

# --- Docs and scratch ----------------------------------------------------
**/ai_docs/
**/arch_test_scripts/
**/*.md
**/CLAUDE.md
